    "chunk_text": "\u201cProvided further that the Minister may from timeto time, having regard to the interests of the nationaleconomy, by Order published in the Gazette\u2013\n\n(a)exempt from the operation of the above levy,any item specified therein; or\n\nShort title.\n\nAmendment ofsection 2 of Part1 of the FinanceAct, No. 11 of2002.\n\n2Finance (Amendment) Act, No. 48 of 2006\n\nEvery Order made in terms of this proviso by theMinister shall\u2014\n\n(i)be in operation immediately upon the Ministeraffixing his signature thereto;\n\n(ii)be published in the Gazette as soon asconvenient;\n\n(iii)be approved by Resolution of Parliament assoon as convenient thereafter; and\n\n(iv)if not approved by Parliament, be deemed tobe rescinded with effect from the date of suchResolution.\u201d.\n\n3.The provisions of this Part shall come into operationfrom January 1, 2007.\n\n4.Part V of the Finance Act, No. 11 of 2006 is herebyamended in section 14, by the substitution for the words andfigures \u201cAct, No. 6 of 2005\u201d of the words \u201cAct, No. 5 of 2005\u201d.\n\n5.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.Sinhala text toprevail in case ofinconsistency.\n\nOperation of Act.\n\nAmendment ofsection 14 of PartV of the FinanceAct, No. 11 of2006.\n\nFinance (Amendment) Act, No. 48 of 20063\n\nAnnual subscription of English Bills and Acts of the Parliament Rs. 885 (Local), Rs. 1,180(Foreign), payable to the SUPERINTENDENT, GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, NO. 32, TRANSWORKSHOUSE, LOTUS ROAD, COLOMBO 01 before 15th December each year in respect of the year following."
