    "chunk_text": "(f)all such sums of money as may be received as thepayment for any courses of study conducted by theInstitute.\u201d.\n\n9.The following new sections are inserted immediatelyafter section 10 of the principal enactment and shallhave effect as sections 10A, 10B, 10C, 10D and 10E of thatenactment :\u2014\n\n10B. The Board may appoint standingcommittees or ad hoc committees as it may deemnecessary for the exercise, performance anddischarge of any of the powers, duties orfunctions of the Board. Such Committees mayinclude persons who are not members of theBoard.\n\n10C. (1) The Board may from time to time admitas members of the Institute, such persons asthe Board considers suitable for admission asmembers.\n\n(2) The Board shall make rules setting outthe criteria for membership, the different classes\n\nInsertion of newsections 10A,10B, 10C, 10Dand 10E in theprincipalenactment.\u201cInternationalAdvisoryCouncil.\n\nAppointmentofCommittees.\n\nMembershipof theInstitute.\n\nSri Lanka Institute of Strategic Studies(Amendment) Act, No. 32 of 20067\n\nand categories of members (including Honorarymembers and Affiliated members), the methodand manner of admission of members, thestructure of fees to be paid by members, therights of members including the right to vote,the obligations of members of each class orcategory and the manner in which persons shallcease to be members of the Institute.\n\n(3) The Board may take such action as theBoard may deem appropriate, against a memberof the Institute, whom the Board deems to haveacted in a manner prejudicial or contrary to theinterests of the Institute.\n\n10D. The Board may make rules in respect ofany or all of the matters specified in the Act.The Board may alter or repeal such rules andmay at any time make new, amended or additionalrules. The rules shall bind the members of theInstitute. Every rule made by the Board shall bepublished in the Gazette."
